{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTailFirstInstance","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTailFirstInstance","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer","lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BinomialSquareSums"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTailFirstInstance.nuV_top_closed_form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTailFirstInstance.nuV_top_closed_form","kind":"theorem","line":168,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramTailFirstInstance.lean#L168-L195","doc":"**The exact closed form**, conditional on the Plancherel normalisation\n`hnorm : tiltNorm k 0 = k!` (the RSK/Burnside identity in this encoding — see the module docstring\nfor the single missing brick):\n\n`ν_n = n(n−2)(n−3)·C(2n−4, n−2) / (3·n!)`,  `n = r + 2`.\n\nEvery other input is proved.\n\n**Cap lifted 2026-08-23.** As with `nuV_top_nonneg`, `hk'` only discharges mean-zero; the uncapped\nrestatement (which also discharges `hnorm`) is\n`SecondMomentKernelVanishes.nuV_top_closed_form`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTailFirstInstance.nuV_top_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTailFirstInstance.nuV_top_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramTailFirstInstance.lean#L137-L166","doc":"**The (TAIL) first instance: `ν_n ≥ 0`** — unconditional on the range where `mean_zero` is\ndischarged (`3 ≤ k ≤ 20`). The numerator's closed form `2k·(k−2)(k−3)·C(2k−4,k−2)/6` is\nnonnegative for `k ≥ 3` and the normalisation is positive, so the quotient is nonnegative. The\n`(k−3)` factor is the exact source of the vanishing at `k = 3`, reproducing the observed ν-pattern\n`-+0` at `n = 3`.\n\n**Cap lifted 2026-08-23.** `hk'` is used only to discharge mean-zero, which now holds for every `k`\n(`SecondMomentKernelVanishes.secondMomentKernel_eq_zero`); the uncapped restatement is\n`SecondMomentKernelVanishes.nuV_top_nonneg`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTailFirstInstance.six_mul_top_numerator","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTailFirstInstance.six_mul_top_numerator","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramTailFirstInstance.lean#L70-L135","doc":"**The top numerator in closed form** (steps 2–5 assembled). With `k = r + 2`,\n\n`6 · Σ_{hook shapes} (f^λ)²·ω₃(λ) = 2(r+2)·r(r−1)·C(2r, r)`.\n\nThe hook shapes carry `f = C(r+1, i)` (`sytDim_hookShape`) and `6ω₃ = 2(r+2)·(3i² − 3(r+1)i +\n(r+1)r)` (`six_mul_omega3_hookShape`); the `C(r+1,i)²`-weighted bracket then collapses\n(`bracket_sum_collapse`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTailFirstInstance.tiltNorm_zero_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTailFirstInstance.tiltNorm_zero_pos","kind":"theorem","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramTailFirstInstance.lean#L57-L68","doc":"The Plancherel normalisation is **positive**: `Σ_λ (f^λ)² > 0` (every dimension is positive on\nthe enumerator, and the enumerator is nonempty for `k ≥ 1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTailFirstInstance.list_sum_map_range_real","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramTailFirstInstance.list_sum_map_range_real","kind":"theorem","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/YoungDiagramTailFirstInstance.lean#L47-L55","doc":"`List.range`-map sum as a `Finset.range` sum (the ℝ twin of\n`YoungDiagramTransposeBridge.list_sum_map_range`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}